  "scope": "At the second FREEZE direction guard, both complementary symbolic branches of the declared two-target domain keep their fourteen constraints when only the resolved guard condition is changed from one to zero. The original branch jumps to the rejection path and rejoins an established exact state; the guard-removed branch falls through with the same frame outside program counter and control. The branches share thirteen constraints and differ only in first <= SUPPLY versus SUPPLY < first. A compiled mutant that removes only this guard is killed by the original rejection consumer at a first target above supply.",
